{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3277","artifact_type":"audit-report","name":"doc-drift-audit-bookend-validator-wiring@sha256:efd1647325fc40859d4f3ff1f3d5a69193ab65656c276f7541237f2e8f4c36c3"},"owner_reference":"3277","content":"# Documentation Drift Audit Report: Bookend-Validator-Wiring\n\n**Generated**: 2026-08-29  \n**Repository**: claude_skills  \n**Issue**: #3277 \u2014 fix: swarm-task-planner does not generate T0/TN bookend tasks for plans with acceptance-criteria-structured\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\n**Total Drift Items**: 1 Critical  \n**Issue**: Documented automatic bookend task generation does not occur in practice.  \n**Root Cause**: The `swarm-task-planner` agent is documented to generate T0/TN bookend tasks whenever a plan contains `acceptance-criteria-structured` entries, but implementation evidence shows this generation is not happening reliably. Plan Pb31107bf had 6 `acceptance-criteria-structured` entries yet generated no T0/TN tasks.\n\n**Impact**: The complete-implementation Pre-Phase 1 TN Verification Check cannot run because the TN-verification artifact is absent. The gate silently treats this absence as \"no structured criteria to verify\" rather than \"structured criteria were never verified.\" This allows implementation to proceed without validating acceptance criteria.\n\n---\n\n## Analyzed Files\n\n### Documentation\n- `/plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` (lines 309-337)\n- `/plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` (lines 328-391, 605-612)\n- `/plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` (lines 300-341)\n- `/plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py` (BookendValidator class)\n\n### Implementation\n- `/plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py` (lines 276-393: BookendValidator validation)\n- Git commits: 5b150f7ac, 9e4b1fc11, a552056b2\n\n---\n\n## Critical Finding: Documented but Unimplemented\n\n### 1. Documented Behavior\n\n**File**: `implement-feature/SKILL.md`  \n**Location**: Section \"Bookend Task Ordering\" (lines 309-337)  \n**Exact Quote**:\n\n```\nWhen the plan contains `acceptance-criteria-structured` entries, `swarm-task-planner` generates T0 and TN bookend tasks. No special handling is needed in this loop \u2014 existing readiness logic dispatches them in the correct order automatically:\n\n- **T0** has `priority: 1` and `dependencies: []`, so it is the first ready task and dispatches before any implementation task.\n- **TN** has `dependencies: [all non-bookend task IDs]`, so it becomes ready only after all implementation tasks complete and dispatches last.\n```\n\n**File**: `swarm-task-planner.md`  \n**Location**: Section \"Bookend Task Generation\" (lines 330-334)  \n**Exact Quote**:\n\n```\nWhen the plan's `acceptance-criteria-structured` field is non-empty, automatically generate two bookend tasks: T0 (baseline capture) and TN (verification gate). These bracket all implementation work.\n\n### Condition\n\nGenerate bookend tasks when and only when the plan contains a non-empty `acceptance-criteria-structured` list. Plans without this field produce no T0/TN tasks and no dependency changes.\n```\n\n**File**: `swarm-task-planner.md`  \n**Location**: Phase 3 Task Decomposition (line 542)  \n**Exact Quote**:\n\n```\nBookend generation: after decomposing implementation tasks, check whether the plan's `acceptance-criteria-structured` field is non-empty. If yes, apply the field sets and dependency rules defined in Bookend Task Generation above.\n```\n\n### 2. Actual Implementation Reality\n\n**Issue #3277 Observation** (2026-08-28/29):\n\n- **Plan ID**: Pb31107bf\n- **Fact 1**: Plan contains `acceptance-criteria-structured` with 6 entries (each with `check-command`, `expected-baseline`, `expected-final`)\n- **Fact 2**: Plan task list is `T1, T2, T3, T4, T5, T6` only \u2014 **NO T0, NO TN**\n- **Issue Statement**: \"swarm-task-planner produced plan Pb31107bf with a populated `acceptance-criteria-structured` list (6 entries, each with a `check-command`, `expected-baseline`, and `expected-final`), but generated no `T0` or `TN` bookend tasks.\"\n\n**Source**: GitHub Issue #3277 description, verified by session observation during `/dh:work-backlog-item work --auto #3268`.\n\n### 3. Validation Layer (Exists but Not Enforced at Generation)\n\n**File**: `/plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py`  \n**Class**: `BookendValidator` (lines 276-393)  \n**Validation Rule 5** (lines 383-391):\n\n```python\n# Rule 5: structured criteria require both bookend tasks\nif self._plan.acceptance_criteria_structured:\n    if t0 is None:\n        errors.append(\n            \"Plan has acceptance-criteria-structured but no T0 baseline task (bookend_type='t0-baseline'). Add a T0 task or remove structured criteria.\"\n        )\n    if tn is None:\n        errors.append(\n            \"Plan has acceptance-criteria-structured but no TN verification task (bookend_type='tn-verification'). Add a TN task or remove structured criteria.\"\n        )\n```\n\n**Status**: This validator CHECKS that bookend tasks exist when structured criteria are present, but it does not GENERATE them. The gap is that the generator (swarm-task-planner agent) is supposed to create the tasks before the validator runs, but the plan was created without them.\n\n### 4. Downstream Consequence\n\n**File**: `complete-implementation/SKILL.md`  \n**Location**: Section \"Pre-Phase 1: TN Verification Check\" (lines 300-341)  \n**Decision Logic** (lines 317-318 Mermaid diagram):\n\n```\nartifact_read(item_id={item_ref}, artifact_type='TN-verification') \u2192 Exists{Artifact exists?}\nExists -->|No| Proceed[\"No structured criteria \u2014 proceed to Phase 1\"]\n```\n\n**Consequence**: When TN-verification artifact is absent, the check treats it as \"No structured criteria \u2014 proceed to Phase 1\" and skips all verification. This is indistinguishable from a plan that genuinely has no structured criteria:\n\n- **Plan with no structured criteria** \u2192 No TN artifact expected \u2192 Proceed (correct)\n- **Plan with structured criteria but no T0/TN tasks** \u2192 No TN artifact exists \u2192 Proceed (incorrect \u2014 verification was never captured)\n\nThe issue statement confirms: \"This is indistinguishable, from the gate's perspective, from a plan that genuinely has no structured criteria to verify \u2014 it does not distinguish 'nothing to check' from 'something to check that was never captured.' The plan's 6 structured criteria therefore never get an independent, empirically-measured before/after comparison.\"\n\n---\n\n## Severity Assessment\n\n| Aspect | Classification |\n|--------|-----------------|\n| **Type** | Implemented-but-Unimplemented Gap |\n| **Severity** | Critical |\n| **Functional Impact** | Acceptance criteria validation is bypassed silently |\n| **Detection** | User-visible: plan lacks expected T0/TN tasks |\n\n---\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\n\nThe BookendValidator exists and correctly validates that structured criteria require bookend tasks. However, **the swarm-task-planner agent is documented to generate these tasks automatically, but that generation is not occurring in practice**.\n\nTwo possible root causes (not investigated, per issue statement):\n\n1. **Agent Logic Gap**: The swarm-task-planner agent code does not implement the bookend generation logic documented in its spec.\n2. **Wiring Gap**: BookendValidator was wired into the plan write path (commit 9e4b1fc11) after swarm-task-planner agent interactions, and the agent may not be using the latest plan creation contract.\n\n**Git Evidence**:\n- Commit `5b150f7ac`: BookendValidator added (feature)\n- Commit `9e4b1fc11`: BookendValidator wired into plan write path (fix \u2014 \"wire BookendValidator into plan write path\")\n- Commit `a552056b2`: Bookend enforcement integration tests added (most recent)\n\nThe integration tests (a552056b2) suggest enforcement is now working, but plan Pb31107bf (generated 2026-08-28/29) still failed to generate T0/TN despite being created after these commits. This suggests the agent itself (swarm-task-planner) may not be using the generation logic.\n\n---\n\n## Recommendations\n\n### Priority 1: Investigate swarm-task-planner Agent Logic\n\n**Action**: Trace swarm-task-planner's actual execution when given a plan with `acceptance-criteria-structured` entries.\n\n**Question**: Does the agent implement lines 542 of its spec? (\"Bookend generation: after decomposing implementation tasks, check whether the plan's `acceptance-criteria-structured` field is non-empty. If yes, apply the field sets and dependency rules...\")\n\n**Files to Inspect**: \n- The swarm-task-planner agent's delegation context and execution logs\n- Session transcript from the run that created Pb31107bf\n\n### Priority 2: Add Pre-Generation Validation\n\n**Action**: Update swarm-task-planner to validate the created plan before returning it.\n\n**Suggested Change**: After creating the plan and before returning the plan ID, call `BookendValidator` to ensure all rules pass. If validation fails, append a concerns block with specifics:\n\n```\n- [ ] CONTRACT: Plan has acceptance-criteria-structured but missing T0 baseline task\n- [ ] CONTRACT: Plan has acceptance-criteria-structured but missing TN verification task\n```\n\nThis surfaces the gap immediately to the user/orchestrator rather than silently allowing a malformed plan.\n\n### Priority 3: Clarify complete-implementation Pre-Phase 1 Logic\n\n**Action**: Update the Pre-Phase 1 check to distinguish between \"no structured criteria\" and \"structured criteria not verified\".\n\n**Current Behavior** (line 318):\n```\nArtifact missing \u2192 \"No structured criteria \u2014 proceed to Phase 1\"\n```\n\n**Suggested Behavior**:\n```\nArtifact missing:\n  IF plan has acceptance_criteria_structured:\n    STOP \u2014 \"Bookend verification was not captured. Run T0 and TN tasks first.\"\n  ELSE:\n    Proceed to Phase 1 (genuinely no criteria)\n```\n\nThis requires reading the plan to check whether `acceptance_criteria_structured` is populated, which is already available via the plan_ref.\n\n---\n\n## Evidence Trail\n\n| Aspect | Evidence | Source |\n|--------|----------|--------|\n| Documentation claim | \"When the plan contains `acceptance-criteria-structured` entries, `swarm-task-planner` generates T0 and TN bookend tasks.\" | implement-feature/SKILL.md:311 |\n| Documentation claim | Bookend generation is automatic when `acceptance-criteria-structured` is non-empty | swarm-task-planner.md:330-334 |\n| Actual behavior | Plan Pb31107bf: 6 criteria entries, 0 T0/TN tasks | Issue #3277 description |\n| Validation exists | BookendValidator Rule 5 enforces bookend requirement | dependencies.py:383-391 |\n| Consequence not addressed | Pre-Phase 1 treats missing TN artifact as \"no criteria\" | complete-implementation/SKILL.md:318 |\n| Integration tests exist | Bookend enforcement tests added | Commit a552056b2 |\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe documentation correctly states that `swarm-task-planner` should generate T0/TN bookend tasks when `acceptance-criteria-structured` is present. The BookendValidator correctly checks this invariant. However, the actual swarm-task-planner agent execution did not generate these tasks for plan Pb31107bf, leading to silent validation bypass in complete-implementation.\n\nThis is a **critical functional drift**: the documented automatic behavior is not implemented, and the downstream verification gate cannot detect the gap."}